00\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u000f\u0000\u0000\u0000\u000f\u0000\u0000\u0000\u000f\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0010\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0010\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0010\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0010\u0000\u0000\u0000\u000f\u0000\u0000\u0000\u000f\u0000\u0000\u0000\u000f\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0015\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u00f6\u00ff\u00e6\u0000R\u0001The Bulldog was an attempt to make a big brother to the very suc"
    },
    {
      "type": "ascii",
      "start": 802,
      "end": 1076,
      "text": "essful Maddog OmniMech, known in the Inner Sphere as the Hagateka, or Vulture.   Though the design was a marginal success, updating the chassis to 75 tons, some critics feel this design is merely a stopgap in attempt to fill holes in the still recovering Clan Forces.   \r\n\r\n"
    },
    {
      "type": "len_string",
      "start": 1076,
      "end": 1850,
      "length": 772,
      "text": "When Rom Agents first brought to attention this variant seen on some battle fields, we had to wonder if the Clan designers were on drugs when they dreamed up this variant.  We could not explain the three Micro Pulse lasers that adorn the right arm, or the 6 slightly larger Medium Pulse Lasers.  After some debate, it was decided this mech was a sharpshooter brawler of sorts.  After all, as we know, pulse lasers are far more accurate than thier ER relatives, though with less range.  The two streak stacks from alternate A are distributed to both Torso's now, so thier is one on each side.   An addition of two AMS systems with a ton of ammo each keeps the fighting fair, as well as Anti personnel pods on the legs.  Some have nicknamed this configuration \"drugged Loki\""
    },
